    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **58 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft delete. Here's what I did:\n\n**Domain model**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `Boolean deleted` field (defaulting to `false`) with getter/setter, mapped to a new `deleted` column.\n\n**API contract & mapping**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (and MapStruct mapping) carries it. A newly created owner serializes `deleted: false`.\n\n**Endpoint behavior**\n- `DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `owner.setDeleted(true)` and saves. The DELETE pipeline still responds 204 (2xx) and the row is retained, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` still returns the owner with `deleted: true`.\n\n**Create-endpoint duplicate/identity checks**\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java` and `CheckPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 now skip any existing owner flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n\n**Database schema/seed**\n- Added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to the owners table in the hsqldb, h2, postgres, and mysql `schema.sql` files.\n- Updated the hsqldb `data.sql` column-less owner inserts to include the new `FALSE` value (the test DB is hsqldb; h2/postgres use column-list inserts so `DEFAULT FALSE` applies; mysql's seed was already independent of its schema and isn't exercised by tests).\n\nThe new checkpoint tests (`Cp46Tests`: soft-delete flags & retains, and deleted owner ignored by the duplicate check) pass, and all 58 tests across the suite remain green.",
